{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"2\u5272\u7279\u4f8b\u30fb3\u5272\u7279\u4f8b\u306e\u671f\u9593\uff08\u8ab2\u7a0e\u671f\u9593\u304c\u5165\u308b\u304b\uff09"},"description":"Japanese consumption tax special rules for small businesses that became taxable because they registered for invoices: the 2\u5272\u7279\u4f8b (pay 20% of output tax) applies to each taxable period that contains any day from 2023-10-01 to 2026-09-30, and the new 3\u5272\u7279\u4f8b (pay 30% of output tax, individuals only) applies to the 2027 and 2028 calendar years. Give a date and the taxpayer type (individual = calendar year; corporation = give the business year start and end) and it says whether that taxable period is inside each window. It only checks the period; whether the other conditions are met (base-period sales of \u00a510 million or less, not taxable anyway, etc.) is for the caller to decide. From the 2026 tax reform law enacted 2026-03-31 (NTA invoice Q&A \u554f114, 114-2).","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"as_of":{"description":"\u8ab2\u7a0e\u671f\u9593\u306b\u542b\u307e\u308c\u308b\u65e5 YYYY-MM-DD\uff082023-10-01\u301c2031-12-31\u3002\u6cd5\u4eba\u306e\u8ab2\u7a0e\u671f\u9593\u304c 2023-10-01 \u3088\u308a\u524d\u306b\u59cb\u307e\u308b\u6642\u306f\u305d\u306e\u521d\u65e5\u304b\u3089\uff09\u3002\u7701\u304f\u3068\u4eca\u65e5\uff08\u65e5\u672c\u6642\u9593\uff09","maxLength":10,"type":"string"},"period_end":{"description":"\u6cd5\u4eba\u306e\u8ab2\u7a0e\u671f\u9593\uff08\u4e8b\u696d\u5e74\u5ea6\uff09\u306e\u672b\u65e5 YYYY-MM-DD","maxLength":10,"type":"string"},"period_start":{"description":"\u6cd5\u4eba\u306e\u8ab2\u7a0e\u671f\u9593\uff08\u4e8b\u696d\u5e74\u5ea6\uff09\u306e\u521d\u65e5 YYYY-MM-DD","maxLength":10,"type":"string"},"taxpayer_type":{"description":"individual\uff1d\u500b\u4eba\u4e8b\u696d\u8005\uff08\u8ab2\u7a0e